      "message": "a8 (54-b): hardness-gated serve blend — honest FAIL of record; gate ships opt-in, default stays v1 law\n\nP-A8 pre-registered under seal v10 (addendum A8: w(ens3)=0|1 on saturation\ns=top.p(ens2), H*=ESCALATE_BELOW=0.55 REUSED, no new constant); runs under\nv10; verdicts + reseal v11 (v9 entry restored into seal_history, append-only).\n\n- P-A8a PASS: 602 wire calls, 551 closed == v1-law byte-identical, 51 open ==\n  registered ens3 (0 mismatches) — the implementation IS the registered rule.\n- P-A8b FAIL: gate opens 11/259 saturated eval calls (min top.p 0.3921); every\n  P-W2b flip sits on a would-escalate row (battery gated 0.9459 == unconditional)\n  — no per-row confidence gate can guarantee whole-slice closure.\n- P-A8c FAIL: shift-H2 gated == ens2 exactly (242/343 = 0.7055, 40 opens,\n  0 flips): all 43 table cells carry G=0 (stream grow deforms gamma=0), the\n  archived prior is a distance-tilted frequency, field arm 61.45-65.67% < heads.\n  Hardness law narrows to FRESH memory only (P-G2d was priorCounted H1 memory).\n- P-A8d PASS: twin core-v2 9960B==9960B re-verified under v10; serve prior\n  rebuild consumes the TWIN table (47 ctx prior vectors identical); smoke 9/9;\n  selftest green; receipt bytes reproduce exactly under the final law.\n\nServe modes: default = v1 law (ens2); serve_with_field = unconditional ens3\n(A7); hardness_gate=true = registered gated blend (A8, opt-in only).\nA9 priced: compile-time soil calibration (train-only) and/or FRESH stream\nmemory in the artifact + real gamma amplitudes. e_a8 added to CI battery.",
